  "environment_caveats": [
    "live_origin is the apex. The client record has no apex_cutover.completed_at, but it does carry cut_over_at=2026-09-22 and the apex serves the current main build over Cloudflare with no x-robots-tag header. The staging alias (staging.rankai-california-restoration-west.pages.dev) still serves the 2026-08-27 build (different CSS hash) and would have audited stale code, so the apex was used. SEO counts toward the verdict this run.",
    "Prior audit (2026-08-26) ran against the staging Pages preview. Regression comparison matches URLs by path across the origin change. SEO deltas (69 -> 100) reflect removal of the staging noindex artifact, not a site change.",
    "Lighthouse ran DESKTOP only (for_mobile=false) for fleet comparability. Mobile performance would typically run 10-20 points lower.",
    "has_micromarkup_errors: DataForSEO flags structured-data validation errors on the 5 pages that render a BreadcrumbList and not on the home page (which does not). The final ListItem in every BreadcrumbList omits the 'item' URL. Google permits this for the last crumb, but stricter validators do not; this is the most likely cause. DataForSEO's instant endpoint does not return the error text, so this is inferred, not confirmed.",
    "Prior run's lighthouse_issues were capped at the top ~6 per URL; this run records all failing audits. 'New issues' such as unused-javascript (GTM gtag.js, present on both builds) and cache-insight may have been failing last month but not captured.",
    "Client record status is 'onboarding', not 'active'. build_status is pushed_main and all 6 URLs returned 200, so the run proceeded. Flagged rather than skipped."
